Business.detail:
Communism Works argues that Republicans dumb down supporters to fear communism. The taboo of communism is fading. Communism is misunderstood as government control. Government Control argues that Government owning means of production is communism. Centralised control of supply chains is communist. Communist government compels allocation of resources. Central control of resources for public benefit is communist.

@dpsl.bsky.social: “Is that communism when the government owns the means of production”

Communism Works (80%) says Communism is a viable system. Government Control (20%) says Government owns means of production.

Technology.detail:
AI Coding argues that AI should not be a user feature. AI-generated code is unavoidable. AI displaces work in time. AI Not Needed argues that AI requires complex operations over vast datasets. AI leads to less code review and lower quality products. AI and vibe coding can wreck existing products and systems.

@bookofoak.bsky.social: “I honestly do not care if AI is used during the coding process, just that it appears nowhere as an *user feature*. Or at least fucking make it opt in.”

AI Coding (76.7%) says AI is used in coding. AI Not Needed (23.3%) says AI is not needed or desired.

Social Media Fails argues that Social media is harmful. Twitter Sucks argues that Twitter is scary now. Twitter is a hellhole. Twitter is making me angry again.

@manzirae.bsky.social: “I'm very late to this realization bc I slowly just stopped using it but twitter is straight up scary now”

Social Media Fails (50.6%) says Social media is harmful. Twitter Sucks (49.4%) says Twitter is scary or unpleasant.

Culture.detail:
Trick Treaters argues that Let kids be kids on Halloween. Few Kids argues that They said the kids were excited but few came. I expected more kids this year but they didn't show. No kids came to our door this year. We told people kids were coming but few did.

@scarnecchia.net: ““Happy Halloween! What are you?” Kid 1 (age 7-8 ish): I’m a banana! (Is clearly a banana) Kid 2 (around the same age): I’m a flowergirl! Who died at the wedding! (is in a dress that is covered in fake blood) Dad, dressed as a banana, quickly: That’s not my kid”

Trick Treaters (81.2%) says Let kids be kids on Halloween. Few Kids (18.8%) says Few kids showed up.
